      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Research suggests that a balanced approach that also acknowledges systemic injustices and power struggles can be more effective in teaching critical thinking, empathy, and social awareness. Balanced curricula that incorporate both national triumphs and challenges can help middle schoolers develop a nuanced understanding of history and its relevance to their lives. This approach can also encourage discussion, debate, and reflection, which are essential skills for informed citizens. By exploring both perspectives, students can gain a deeper understanding of the complexities of history and its ongoing impact.",
